From fcd4205e6ed65e4abeca12af1dad05f316f5c958 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Donham <j.donham@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 23:43:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix Fountain parser and HTML escaping; polish
 autocomplete

Parser
- Recognise character cues carrying an extension. "JOHN (V.O.)" and
  "MARY (O.S.)" were parsed as action because the \b in the extension
  regex can never match before a closing paren, so off-screen and
  voice-over cues never formatted.
- End a dialogue block at a blank line, as Fountain requires. The old
  parser walked back over blank lines, so any action paragraph following
  dialogue was rendered as dialogue.
- Require cues to be uppercase, preceded by a blank line and followed by
  a non-blank line. Title case previously qualified, so ordinary action
  ("The door opens slowly.") was formatted as a character cue. Fountain's
  "@" prefix forces a cue for names that are not uppercase.
- Allow periods in cues only inside abbreviations, so "MRS. SMITH" and
  "J.R." parse while a sentence ending in a full stop does not.
- Rebuild the character/location vocabulary on each parse instead of
  accumulating it, so half-typed names stop polluting autocomplete.

Escaping
- escapeHtml now escapes quotes, making it safe in attribute values.
- Build the presets list and autocomplete items with DOM calls. A preset
  named 'JOE"S BAR' used to break out of data-preset and corrupt the
  markup.
- Escape the title, author and contact fields in the preview, and the
  title in the PDF export document.

Autocomplete
- Position the popup at the caret rather than a fixed +100px offset from
  the editor, clamped to the viewport and flipped above when short of
  room. Switch to position: fixed to avoid pane clipping.
- Add keyboard navigation (arrows, Enter/Tab to accept, Escape to close)
  using the .selected style that was already defined but unused.
- Filter by prefix with dedupe, a two-character minimum and an eight-item
  cap, instead of substring-matching on every keystroke.

Other
- Quick insert selects its placeholder and adds only the missing blank
  line, instead of always prepending two newlines.
- Trigger printing even when the export window is already complete, and
  report a blocked pop-up instead of failing silently.
- Wrap localStorage writes so a full or disabled store cannot break
  autosave or the beforeunload handler.
- Add the MIT LICENSE the README badge advertises; replace the
  yourusername placeholder URLs, correct the local-dev steps and document
  the formatting rules and shortcuts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AGrCfSuQ1C8phGhiRMZ9Wh
