From 768113b81b7db9af0df6ba2aa11811d54819e259 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Donham <j.donham@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 23:51:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Insert quick-insert elements after the caret line, never
 inside it

Clicking Character, Scene, Transition or Parenthetical with the caret
mid-word split the line: "MAY|A" became "MAY", the new element, then a
stray "A". Insertion now happens at the end of the caret's line, so the
line the writer is on is left intact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AGrCfSuQ1C8phGhiRMZ9Wh
